{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Listen, [Eb]I tell you a mys[Bb]tery, it is [Cm]written in the word
We will [Ab]not all sleep, but the [Eb]trumpet will be [Bb]heard
In [Cm]an instant, in the blink of an [Ab]eye
The [Bb]dead will be raised impe[Ab]rishable, [Bb]and we will be [Eb]changed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Where, O death, is [Bb]your victory
[Cm]Where, O death, is your [Ab]sting
[Eb]Death has been swallowed up [Bb]in victory
[Cm]But thanks be to God, [Ab]who gives us the vic[Bb]tory
Through our Lord Jesus [Eb]Christ
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Every body that [Bb]is breaking, every [Cm]friend we laid to rest
Will [Ab]put on the imperishable [Eb]and rise up from the [Bb]dust
[Cm]The sting of death is [Ab]sin, and the power of sin is the [Bb]law
But the victory is given us, the [Ab]grave has lost its claw
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Where, O death, is [Bb]your victory
[Cm]Where, O death, is your [Ab]sting
[Eb]Death has been swallowed up [Bb]in victory
[Cm]But thanks be to God, [Ab]who gives us the vic[Bb]tory
Through our Lord Jesus [Eb]Christ
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
For the [Bb]trumpet will sound
And the [Cm]dead will be raised impe[Ab]rishable
And [Bb]we will be changed
[Cm]This mortal body [Ab]must put on immortali[Bb]ty
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Where, O death, is your [Bb]sting
[Cm]Thanks be to [Abmaj7]God
{end_of_verse}

